---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { COMPANY, LICENCE, PRIVACY, REPO } from "../config";
---

<Legal
  title="Legal notice — GitWarren"
  description="Who operates gitwarren.com: Klarluft B.V., its registration details, and the terms under which the site and the GitWarren app are provided."
  eyebrow="Legal notice"
  heading="Who is behind this site."
  intro="EU rules entitle you to know who is running an online service before you download anything from it. This page says who we are and how to reach us."
>
  <h2>Operator</h2>

  <!-- The legal name ends in a full stop, so never end a sentence with it. -->
  <p>
    This website and the GitWarren desktop app are published by {
      COMPANY.legalName
    }, a company registered in the Netherlands.
  </p>

  <dl>
    <dt>Company</dt>
    <dd>{COMPANY.legalName}</dd>

    <dt>Registered address</dt>
    <dd>{COMPANY.address}</dd>

    <dt>Chamber of Commerce</dt>
    <dd>KvK {COMPANY.kvk}</dd>

    <dt>VAT number</dt>
    <dd>{COMPANY.vat}</dd>

    <dt>Email</dt>
    <dd><a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a></dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>The software</h2>

  <p>
    GitWarren is free software, released under the <a href={LICENCE} rel="noopener"
      >GNU General Public License, version 3</a
    >. That licence — not this page — governs your use of the app, including its
    terms on copying, modification and the absence of any warranty. The source is
    at <a href={REPO} rel="noopener">github.com/klarluft/gitwarren-app</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>

  <p>
    The pages here describe what the app does and point at its releases. We keep
    them accurate and check every claim against the app itself, but the site is
    provided as it is, with no warranty, and we are not liable for any loss
    arising from relying on it. Downloads are served by GitHub, whose availability
    is not ours to promise.
  </p>

  <p>
    The GitWarren name, logo and the text and design of this site belong to {
      COMPANY.legalName
    }, and are not covered by the app's GPL licence. The screenshots show the app
    itself.
  </p>

  <h2>Links out</h2>

  <p>
    Where this site links elsewhere — GitHub above all — the content on the other
    end is not ours and not something we can vouch for.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>

  <p>
    What the site and the app collect, which is close to nothing, is set out in
    the <a href={PRIVACY}>privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting in touch</h2>

  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> for anything on
    this page. Bugs
    and feature requests are better filed as <a href={`${REPO}/issues`} rel="noopener"
      >issues on the repository</a
    >, where they are public and get tracked.
  </p>
</Legal>
